#AUTO 37
#NEEDED 0
# i2c0 bus liveness scan (issue 110n).
#
# Walks every 7-bit address on i2c0 and logs which ones respond. The value is
# LIVENESS, not discovery: "is the chip still answering?" A device that responds
# but misbehaves (say a controller that ACKs but its downstream is dead) is a
# more hopeful failure than one gone silent — that distinction is actionable.
# Which address is which is decoded from the board device tree (0x20 = RK817
# PMIC). Reuses the working i2c0 read path; read-only intent. Runs after the
# PMIC probes (@30-36) so i2c0 is known-good first.

CALL i2c_scan
